# ndm_file-timestamp.conf.example - template for NDM File Timestamp (ndm_file-timestamp.sh)
#
# How to use it:
#   1. Copy this file next to the script, removing ".example":
#        cp ndm_file-timestamp.conf.example ndm_file-timestamp.conf
#   2. Edit ndm_file-timestamp.conf: uncomment (remove the leading "#") only the lines
#      you want to change, and replace the example values with yours.
#
# Rules:
#   - One KEY=value per line. Quotes are optional: KEY="a b" and KEY=a b are the same.
#   - Lines starting with "#" are ignored. A commented or missing key keeps its default.
#   - This file is only read, never executed: commands written here are not run.
#   - ndm_file-timestamp.conf is personal: it is listed in .gitignore. Only this template
#     belongs in the repository.
#   - A setting given in the environment wins over this file, and the command line wins
#     over both (for example -d wins over OUTPUT_DIR).
#   - An invalid value stops the script with exit code 2 and says which setting is wrong.

# Folder where the proofs are saved, listed and searched: relative to the script folder,
# or an absolute path such as /media/backup/proofs. -d on the command line wins.
# The proofs already saved next to the script are still found by --verify.
# Default: ndm_file-timestamp-proofs next to the script
#OUTPUT_DIR=/media/backup/proofs

# Folder where --archive creates the archives: relative to the script folder, or an
# absolute path. Created if missing.
# Default: ndm_file-timestamp-archives next to the script
#ARCHIVE_DIR=/media/backup/archives

# Time Stamping Authorities to ask, space or comma separated, among:
#   freetsa   https://freetsa.org            free public TSA
#   digicert  http://timestamp.digicert.com  used worldwide for code signing
#   sectigo   http://timestamp.sectigo.com   used worldwide for code signing
# Default: all three
#TSAS="freetsa digicert sectigo"

# How many different TSAs must confirm a file: when stamping, the run fails with fewer
# timestamps than this; with --verify and --archive, the file fails with fewer different
# TSAs having a valid timestamp. From 1 to the number of TSAs in TSAS. A higher value
# gives a stronger proof, but one TSA out of service is then enough to fail.
# Default: 1
#MIN_TIMESTAMPS=2

# Before stamping, verifying or archiving, compare this script with the one published on
# GitHub for its version (as --check-script does): on stops if they differ, and only warns
# when the comparison is not possible (no network, version not published). It contacts
# GitHub at every run. See "Checking the script" in the README for the independent check.
# Default: off
#SCRIPT_CHECK=on

# Colors on the terminal: on or off. Output saved to a file or sent through a pipe never
# has colors. The NO_COLOR environment variable (https://no-color.org) also turns them off.
# Default: on
#COLORS=off
